course: dictionary
lesson: 6787
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Orb can mean a round ball, a golden ball held by a king, the sun or a planet in a poem, or a glowing ball in a game. To know which one is right, read the words around it. «The king held a golden orb with a cross on top at the coronation.» The words king, golden and coronation tell you the orb is the royal ball, not a game prize.
explain: Poems often use orb to mean the sun or moon. Games use it for a glowing ball you collect. Ask yourself: where am I reading this? Is it a story, a history book, a poem or a game? Then pick the meaning that fits that place.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The orb web glittered with dew.» An orb web is a round spider's web, not a ball. The word web and the spider's sticky spiral make the meaning clear.
fact: An orb is a round ball or object, often one that glows.
fact: «Orb» can mean the golden ball with a cross on top, held by a king or queen at a coronation.
fact: In poems, «orb» can mean the sun, the moon, a planet or an eye.
fact: In video games, an orb is a glowing ball you collect for points or power.
fact: An orb web is a wheel of strong spokes with a sticky spiral that catches flying insects; a garden spider often builds a new one nearly every day.
exercise: «The king held a golden orb with a cross on top at the coronation.» What is the orb? | A pair of golden shoes | *A golden ball with a cross on top, held at a coronation | A small wooden boat | A type of spider's web
exercise: «On an autumn morning a garden fence can glitter with a wheel of dew drops: that is an orb web.» What is an orb web? | *A wheel of sticky silk that catches flying insects | A ball of wool for knitting | A bell that rings at a coronation | A round glowing ball you collect for points
exercise: «Mia collected a glowing orb in the game and won ten extra points.» What is an orb in this sentence? | *A glowing ball you collect for points or power | A stone wall around a castle | A sleepy cat | The sun setting over the sea
test: «The poet wrote that the orb of the sun sank into the sea.» What does orb mean here? | *The sun | A crown | A round book | A small fish
test: «Orb weavers build a fresh round web, often every day or night.» How often do orb weavers build a new web? | Never, they keep one web for life | Only in winter | Once a year | *Often, every day or night
exam: «The Sovereign's Orb is part of the crown jewels, held by the monarch at the coronation.» What is the Sovereign's Orb? | A garden spider | A glowing prize in a video game | *A golden ball with a cross on top, held by the monarch | Dew drops on a web
